From 8f46c0ad1f92e99777338179ed99df5615668582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:01:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cast): WebRTC mirroring + device-auth replay for Quest
 Chromecast

Adds the streaming half of the Cast receiver so a Quest sender can move past
discovery/launch into an actual mirrored picture.

- CastAuth: device-auth replay (embedded Shanocast tuple) + TLS peer cert
- CastWebRtcManager: PeerConnection, OFFER/ANSWER, ICE, video-track render
- CastMirrorActivity: full-screen immersive renderer for the remote video
- CastReceiver: NS_DEVICEAUTH -> auth response, NS_WEBRTC -> offer/ICE wiring
- build.gradle: add org.webrtc:google-webrtc dependency
- AndroidManifest: register CastMirrorActivity

Known issue: org.webrtc:google-webrtc:1.0.32006 was published only to the
now-defunct JCenter, so it will not resolve from the declared google() /
mavenCentral() repos without either adding the .aar to app/libs or switching
to a Maven-Central-hosted WebRTC artifact.

